eal-time data infrastructure. Founding CTO of Curesh. Creator of Keel — open source Go microservices framework.\n- Data Engineering (ETL/ELT, data pipelines)\n- AI/LLM based development (MCP, agents, ADK, CrewAI, etc)\n- Other (SQL, Redis, Docker, AWS, GCP, Azure, DBT)\nData/Backend/Agentic AI engineer for the past ten years (Java, Python, SQL). Experience building data platforms (from scratch!) and ELT pipelines for financial data. Currently working on agentic AI projects, but happy to work at any level for any problem that needs solving.Happy to work on product management, solutions architecture, agentic AI or customer engineering. Remote is preferred for time zones spanning Europe to India, or early hours of EST/PST; onsite/hybrid in Mumbai is also great. Unfortunately cannot relocate.Open primarily to freelance/consulting roles, but full-time roles will also be considered if we're a good fit.\nLocation: Mumbai, India | Remote: Yes | Willing to relocate: Yes (with visa support) | Type: Full-timeProduct Engineer with 3 years building AI-native products end-to-end at Mosaic Wellness (health-tech).Things I've shipped without being asked:\n- Agentic AI support bot: noticed 50% of conversations were escalating to humans. Specced, built, shipped solo. Handoffs now at 23%. Scaling across brands.\n- A/B testing platform: no structured way to test product page changes existed. Built end-to-end. 1% direct revenue lift. Scaling across brands.Side projects:\n- owthorize (npm) — AST-based gate for AI agent tool calls. Catches prompt-injected DDL, unbounded mutations, SSRF, and shell abuse before they execute — without relying on prompt safeguards. 300+ downloads. https://www.npmjs.com/package/owthorize\n- SnoopSignal — Reddit pain discovery tool for solopreneurs. Acquired for $3,000.\n- SQLPremierLeague — SQL learning platform using IPL/NBA/PL/UCL/F1 data. 700+ users, 50–80 DAUs.Stack: TypeScript, React, React Native, Node.js, Python, SQL, LLM APIs, Agentic AI.I work best at 