youtube.com/@typecodelearn6971) obviously my skills have increased considerably since then. I like deep slow work, things that take a few days to a few hours to solve - That being said I am open to everything, if you want it made, I probably can make it.Résumé/CV: See it on my website : https://river.berlinEmail : hackernews@river.berlin (or alternatively use the form on my website)I've 7 years of experience - I started of building services for individuals, and then moved on to ML-related work. I worked at RunPod last, directly working with a number of clients for runpod (including OpenAI, Cursor, Perplexity).\nLocation: Ahmedabad, Gujarat, IndiaRemote: Yes (preferred)Relocation: No, open to occasional onsite visitsTechnologies: NestJS, Node.js, TypeScript, Angular, React, React Native, Ionic, Flutter, MongoDB, PostgreSQL, MySQL, Redis, Docker, AWS, Google Cloud Platform, REST APIs, GraphQL, Microservices, WebSockets, CI/CD, GitHub ActionsExperience: 14+ years as a Full Stack Software Engineer / Software Architect specializing in SaaS products, scalable backend systems, web applications, and cross-platform mobile applications. I have led end-to-end development, designed scalable architectures, optimized system performance, and worked closely with product and engineering teams to deliver production-ready solutions.Résumé/CV: https://www.linkedin.com/in/piyush-patel-32a1b059/Email: piyushpatel.ppp@gmail.comI'm currently open to Full-Time, Contract, or Freelance opportunities. I'm particularly interested in building scalable SaaS platforms, AI-powered applications, CRM systems, workflow automation tools, and cloud-native solutions.If you think my background matches your needs, I'd be happy to connect and discuss how I can contribute to your team.\nLocation: Ontario, CanadaRemote: YesWilling to relocate: NoTechnologies: TypeScript, Deno, Node, BASH, Guile, Preact, React, Vue, GraphQL, Docker, Flatpak, Tailwind, CSS, HTML, Git, Amazon Web Services, Linux, GuixRésumé/CV: 