ce and deep tech. Current research includes building highly performant realtime rendering solutions for the web. Think global illumination at 60fps in the browser.Résumé/CV: <on request>Email: h4chikuku [at] gmail\nTechnologies: .NET (8 years) Expo-React Native (4 years) Next.js-React (3 years)\nI prefer remote work, but relocation is possible. If I relocate to a country where people speak Spanish, Arabic, or Japanese, I'm willing to learn those languages.\nLocation: San Francisco, CARemote: Yes, open to remote or hybridContract: YesTechnologies: LLMs, agentic systems, RAG, semantic search, recommendation systems, computer vision, workflow automation, Python, TypeScript, React, Node.js, PostgreSQL, Kubernetes, Docker, AWS, GCPRésumé/CV: linkedin.com/in/carloschinchilla | github.com/calufa | medium.com/@calufaEmail: calufa@gmail.comStaff AI Engineer / former CTO with 20+ years of software experience and 10+ years building AI systems across LLMs, agentic workflows, semantic search, recommendation systems, computer vision, generative media, and infrastructure.I have built and led multiple zero-to-one AI products, including a WhatsApp finance copilot, invoice automation platform, AI-powered budgeting app, dental computer-vision product, text-to-video AI platform, recommendation infrastructure, and semantic search systems.I was previously CTO at YC and Techstars-backed startups, and two companies I helped build were later acquired by OpenAI and LDC/private equity.Recently, I have been focused on AI-native workflow platforms, company-brain systems, agentic search, LLM tool use, sandboxed execution, structured outputs, evaluation, human-in-the-loop workflows, and AI systems that turn messy business processes into reliable software.\nI'm the one who made the project featured in https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48704289Incoming 4th-year CS major @ GT, looking for contract work (~20 hours a week) from May 2026 - Aug 2027. Especially interested in robotics, RL / embodied ML opportunities; security engineering background. Internships: 2x Apple, SpaceX, SamsungLocation: Atlanta, GA, USARemote: YesWilling to relocate: Yes, after grad. Need to be in ATL for the school yearTechnologies: Python, PyTorch, MuJoCo, PufferLib, reinforcement learning (PPO), C#, Java, JavaScript/TypeScript, SQL, Linux, Kubernetes, WiresharkRésumé/CV: https://karolina.mgdubiel.com and https://linkedin.com/in/karolinadubiel -- please email for actual resume :)Email: karolina+hn [at] mgdubiel (dot) com\nLocation: Brazil (UTC-3) Remote: Yes (remote only, US timezone overlap) Willing to relocate: No Technologies: Rust (Tokio, Axum, Tonic, WASM),Node.js/NestJS/TypeScript, React, PostgreSQL, Redis, RabbitMQ, Docker, AWS/GCP, zk-SNARKs Résumé/CV: https://www.ovasylenko.com Email: hello@ovasylenko.com\nBackend & systems engineer, 18+ years. Two recent builds: Rust — Solo-built Orch8 (orch8.io), a durable workflow orchestration engine. 2,400+ instances/sec, <3ms latency. 7 crates, 3 SDKs (Node/Python/Go), 200+ integrations, built-in LLM tool calling and ReAct agent loops.Node.js/NestJS — Matching engine for a crypto exchange processing 4,000+ orders/sec with sub-millisecond latency. Liquidity bots, candle engine, real-time WebSocket trading.Also: zk-SNARK wallet engine at Panther Protocol (cross-chain, UTXO model), micro-frontend migration at PropertyGuru (4 product teams). Led 15 engineers across 3 time zones.Looking for: Senior/Staff Rust systems, backend architecture (Node.js or Rust), Web3/protocol engineering, or AI infrastructure roles. I care about product ownership and shipping - not process theater.\nLocation: Sarawak, MalaysiaRemote: YesWilling to relocate: NoTechnologies: PHP, Python, Golang, CodeIgniter, SQLite, MySQLI'm good at PHP web development, especially CodeIgniter. One of my prominent work is an IT inventory and asset management. I'm also very familiar with Windows GPO, Powershell and Active Directory.Résumé/CV: mohdshahrim.github.ioEmail: shahrim.private@gmail.com\nLocation: Bengaluru (Bangalore), India | Remote: Yes | Willing to relocate: NegotiableTechnologies:\n> Programming Languages: JavaScript / TypeScript, Python, Go\n> Frontend Development: React.JS, Next.JS, Vue.JS, Astro\n> Backend Development: Node.JS, Express.JS, Django, Flask, Gin\n> Databases: MongoDB, MySQL, PostgreSQL\n> Tools and Platforms: Git, GitHub Actions, Docker, AWS, Vercel, Netlify, CloudflareRésumé/CV: https://linkinseconds.com/p/vachan-mn |\nEmail: contact@vachanmn.techI am a Full-Stack Engineer with experience designing, building, and deploying web applications from scratch. On the frontend, I specialize in React, Next.js, and Astro. On the backend, I build performant APIs and microservices using Node.js (Express/Hono), Go (Gin), and Python (Django/Flask). I have practical experience managing relational and non-relational databases (PostgreSQL, MongoDB) and automate deployments using Git, Docker, GitHub Actions, and AWS/Cloudflare. Seeking full-time roles in full-stack, frontend, or backend engineering.\nLocation: UK/India.Remote: Yes/mostly. Can travel to London either semi-regularly or on a need-basis.Willing to relocate: open.Technologies: C++, C, Python, Rust, Java, Javascript, Typescript, Haskell, Elm, React, Shell script.Resume: https://is.gd/jeenuv_resumeEmail: See resume.Headline: Strong system software and low-level background. Currently works in low-latency/high-frequency trading. Interests: low-level programming, functional programming, distributed systems, formal modelling, web UI tooling, command-line. Open to opportunities in system software or anything adjacent to my expressed interests.\nTechnologies: JavaScript/TypeScript, Node.js, Express.js, React.JS, Next.JS, PostgreSQL\nEmail: vishantagarwal93@gmail.comBackend Engineer with 10+ years of experience building production-grade Node.js and TypeScript APIs, billing systems,and automation pipelines. Owned the billing and metering backend for a high-scale Solana developer