      "title": "Manufact (YC S25) Is Hiring a Developer Advocate in SF",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/manufact/jobs/4cyWd6S-developer-advocate-partnerships-devrel\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48746331\nPoints: 0\n# Comments: 0",
      "body": "Cloud infrastructure for MCP servers and Claude / ChatGPT apps.Developer Advocate & Partnerships (DevRel)$100K - $160K•0.10% - 0.70%•San Francisco, CA, US / RemoteRoleEngineering, Full stackExperienceAny (new grads ok)Connect directly with founders of the best YC-funded startups.Apply to role ›About the roleAbout us\nManufact is Vercel for MCP.\nWe are building the MCP cloud platform to get any product ready for Claude Connectors marketplace, ChatGPT App Store and any AI agent that supports MCP.\nManufact Cloud usage is more than doubling every month.\nWe're the team behind mcp-use SDK (next.js for MCP), the open-source framework for building MCP Apps with 10k Github stars and 8M+ downloads across python and typescript.\nUsed by 20% of US 500 like NASA, SAP, NVIDIA and more than 5,000 companies.\nWe raised $6.3M seed in 4 days before YC demo day. Our lead investor is PeakXV (best dev-tools VC out there), and we have the best angels, including the founders of Supabase.\nOur focus: capture a significant share of global AI tool calls that flow through Manufact.\nWe're looking for a Developer Advocate who also owns partnerships with other dev tools / SDKs end-to-end.\nThis role blends technical storytelling with building real integrations and real relationships across the AI dev-tools ecosystem.\nOne week you're shipping a demo that connects the mcp-use SDK or Manufact Cloud to a partner's product, the next you're on stage at a meetup, then writing the blog post and docs that make it all land.\nYou'll run several efforts in parallel and set the pace yourself.\nIdentify collaboration opportunities with other dev tools and AI infra companies, reach out, and drive each one from first conversation to shipped result.\nBuild demos and integrations between the mcp-use SDK / Manufact Cloud and partner products.\nCreate and publish technical content across formats: videos, demos, GitHub examples, blog posts, and docs.\nMove multiple partnership and content efforts forward at once, owning the timeline for each.\nCollaborate with engineering and marketing to shape how we position technical features and communicate product value.\nRepresent Manufact at technical conferences, meetups, and podcasts, and bring developer feedback back to the team.\nHelp define and evolve our developer-facing voice, presence, and community strategy as we scale.\nStrong software engineering fundamentals. You're comfortable building demos, integrations, and lightweight apps on your own.\nExceptional written and verbal communication. You can make complex technical topics clear and compelling.\nComfortable creating content across written, video, and live formats.\nSelf-directed. You can run several workstreams in parallel without being managed.\nBased in or willing to relocate to San Francisco.\nYou've used the mcp-use SDK / tried Manufact before applying.\nHands-on experience with MCP, agents, or generative AI. Contributions to modelcontextprotocol/* or MCP servers you've built are a strong signal.\nExisting credibility in developer communities (active on X/GitHub, a personal blog, OSS you maintain, talks you've given).\nExperience running partnerships, integrations, or co-marketing with other companies.\nPrior developer advocacy, DevRel, or developer-facing engineering experience.\nWhat you can expect at Manufact\nBurn a lot of tokens\nPremium medical + dependent coverage\nSmall, trusting team of senior + staff engineers\nAbout the interviewHow we hire\nTell us about you and about things you’re proud of (share URLs).\nRecord a short video (1–3 minutes) introducing yourself? Nothing polished\nIntro call with a founder.\nShort take-home: build a demo or integration and the content piece that ships with it.\nAbout ManufactManufact provides open-source dev tools and infrastructure for MCP to help dev teams quickly build and deploy MCP Servers for AI agents & MCP Apps for ChatGPT and Claude.\nWe developed the mcp-use SDK, which has over 7M downloads and 10,000 GitHub stars, and is used by 20% of the US 500.\nCreate MCP servers/apps in minutes, connect your GitHub repo, and make them immediately available to AI agents and ChatGPT.Founded:2025Batch:S25Team Size:5Status:ActiveLocation:San FranciscoFounders",
