      "id": "hackernews-2026-06-30-show-hn-my-13-year-old-built-an-ant-colony-tracker",
      "title": "Show HN: My 13-year-old built an ant colony tracker",
      "summary": "He's 13 years old. He wanted to track his own ant colonies — growth, feeding, humidity, and other metrics. He built the whole app himself with some help from AI tools; I just helped him deploy it to a server. Would love to hear your feedback!\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48735446\nPoints: 34\n# Comments: 25",
      "body": "No sign-up required — try it nowRegister, monitor and care for your ant colonies in one place. Worker history, care calendar, detailed statistics and more.How it worksA complete app for myrmecologists, from beginners to experts.01 — DashboardAll your colonies\nat a glanceYour main panel shows the status of each colony instantly. Worker count, species and quick access to any data you need.✓ Key data cards for each colony✓ Create a new colony in seconds✓ Clean view without clutter02 — Colony detailHistory and evolution\nin chartsEach colony has its own page with a worker evolution chart, brood status, formicarium type and complete feeding log.✓ Worker count chart over time✓ Brood status: eggs, larvae, pupae…✓ Complete feeding history03 — RegisterAdd a colony\nin secondsSimple form to record all the important data: species, queen capture date, formicarium type and brood status.✓ Database with hundreds of species✓ Auto-fill of species information✓ Works without creating an accountEverything you needNo subscriptions. No complications.📊StatisticsEvolution charts for your entire collection, broken down by colony and species.📅CalendarAutomatic feeding and cleaning reminders for each colony.🌍MultilingualAvailable in Spanish, English, French, German and Italian.No sign-upTry the app without an account. Create one to save your data permanently.Ready to start?Enter directly or create your free account to save your data forever.",
