      "id": "hackernews-2026-06-30-knoppix",
      "title": "Knoppix",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://www.knopper.net/knoppix/index-en.html\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48732056\nPoints: 296\n# Comments: 109",
      "body": "KNOPPIX is a bootable Live system on CD, DVD or USB flash drives, consisting of a representative collection of GNU/Linux software, automatic hardware detection, and support for many graphics cards, sound cards, SCSI and USB devices and other peripherals. KNOPPIX can be used as a productive Linux system for the desktop, educational CD, rescue system, or adapted and used as a platform for commercial software product demos. It is not necessary to install anything on a hard disk. Due to on-the-fly decompression, the CD can have up to 2 GB of executable software installed on it (over 9GB on the DVD \"Maxi\" edition).",
